From 091e6fd7d3a9ecdda624d4fe4f9ecef2116217ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:34:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: an output kept on for its sound is asked of
 the driver first, and found by its atomic state

The outputs that hades-keep-outputs names (the commit before this one) were
left on in two ways that nothing checked:

- On the device that Kodi uses, the CRTC of such an output stayed on with its
  planes detached, in the same commit as Kodi's frame and as the turning off of
  the other unused outputs. A driver that does not keep a CRTC on with no plane
  refuses that whole commit, which falls back to the request before it: the
  other outputs then stayed on for good (the turning off was never asked for
  again), the kept one as it was.
- On another device, the CRTC of the output was found through the connector's
  encoder_id only: where a driver leaves it 0 the output was turned off with
  the others, and nothing said so. Nor was an entry of the file that names no
  output ("HDMI-1" for "HDMI-A-1") ever told.

Read in the drivers of this build (Linux 7.3.1, nvidia-open 615.78.08):
amdgpu refuses a CRTC that is on without its primary plane
(amdgpu_dm_crtc_helper_atomic_check(): "Can't enable a CRTC without enabling
the primary plane"), which Kodi knows as QUIRK_NEEDSPRIMARY; i915 and xe (the
same display code) keep a pipe on with no plane (they handle active_planes == 0,
gen2 only turns its underrun reports off for it); nvidia-drm asks nothing of the
planes of a CRTC (nv_drm_crtc_atomic_check()) and gives NVKMS a layer without a
surface as disabled. None of this is taken on trust: the driver is asked.

On the device that Kodi uses, where an output is kept on, the turning off of
the others is now asked first in a request of its own (TEST_ONLY), in this
order (KEEP_OUTPUTS::KeepModes()): the kept output black, with its planes
detached (not with QUIRK_NEEDSPRIMARY); as it was, with what it showed; and
last off, as without the file, so that the other outputs never stay on because
one is kept. The first way that the driver takes goes out with the frame. A
commit that carried the turning off and was refused (its test, or the commit)
asks for it again 10 s later, three times at most for a mode; this also holds
without the file, where the request is the one of before, property for property. A move
to another output (TestOutputMove()) asks the same ways in the same order, and
its commit goes with the one that the driver took; the output that Kodi leaves
goes off as it always did. Nothing is asked again when nothing would change:
the outputs kept on are told once, and again only when that changes.

On another device the CRTC of the output is the one that its atomic state
names (the connector's CRTC_ID, read on a handle that asks for atomic
modesetting, which changes nothing else: the outputs are turned off with the
legacy call as before), and the one of its encoder where the driver has no
atomic modesetting (KEEP_OUTPUTS::CrtcOfOutput()). An output named in the file
that drives nothing is said so, with whether a display is connected.

Once per start, each entry of the file that names none of the outputs of the
devices that drive a display is told, with the names of those outputs.

kodi.log, at info level unless a warning is said:
  "turning off N output(s) not used by Kodi" (as before)
  "DP-1 stay(s) on, black, for its sound (hades-keep-outputs)"
  "DP-1 stay(s) on as it was, with what it showed, for its sound
   (hades-keep-outputs; the driver needs a plane on a CRTC that is on)" (amdgpu)
  "... (hades-keep-outputs; the driver did not take it on with nothing on it:
   <error>)"
  warning "DP-1 go(es) off although hades-keep-outputs keeps it on: the driver
   would take turning off the outputs Kodi does not use only with it (<error>)"
  warning "the commit that turns off the outputs not used by Kodi was refused
   (<error>): it is asked for again in 10 s" / "... refused 3 times (<error>):
   they stay on"
  "/dev/dri/card1: HDMI-A-1 stay(s) on as it was, for its sound
   (hades-keep-outputs)"
  "/dev/dri/card1: DP-2 (hades-keep-outputs) drives nothing now (nothing
   connected, no CRTC in its atomic state): nothing to keep on"
  warning "hades-keep-outputs: "hdmi-1" names none of the outputs of the
   graphics devices that drive a display (card1-HDMI-A-1, ...): nothing is
   kept on for it"

Tested on the host: the parser, the report of entries that name nothing, the
order of the ways and the choice of the CRTC (50 checks; ten mutations of the
header, each caught). The rest is read and syntax-checked against the build's
own compile commands; whether each driver takes each way, and what the
receiver hears, only hardware shows.
